                <p>The present invention relates to a an organic electroluminescent device comprising at least one light-emitting layer B composed of one or more sublayers, wherein the one or more sublayers of the light-emitting layer B as a whole comprise at least one host material H&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;B&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt;, at least one phosphorescence material P&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;B&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt;, at least one small FWHM emitter S&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;B&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt;, and optionally at least one TADF material E&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;B&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt;, wherein S&amp;lt;sup&amp;gt;B&amp;lt;/sup&amp;gt; is a specific boron-containing emitter.</p>
